1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,134
Cyber safety.

2
00:00:01,134 --> 00:00:03,582
Five things every student must know.

3
00:00:04,182 --> 00:00:04,607
First,

4
00:00:04,607 --> 00:00:06,376
digital arrest is a scam.

5
00:00:06,376 --> 00:00:09,420
No police officer or agency arrests anyone,

6
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:10,623
or demands money,

7
00:00:10,623 --> 00:00:12,534
over a phone or video call.

8
00:00:13,134 --> 00:00:13,455
Next,

9
00:00:13,455 --> 00:00:14,801
scammers create fear,

10
00:00:14,801 --> 00:00:17,110
urgency and secrecy. Pause, hang up,

11
00:00:17,110 --> 00:00:19,034
and talk to someone you trust.

12
00:00:19,634 --> 00:00:19,999
Also,

13
00:00:19,999 --> 00:00:21,533
never share your OTP,

14
00:00:21,533 --> 00:00:23,287
UPI PIN or card details.

15
00:00:23,287 --> 00:00:26,063
You never need a PIN to receive money.

16
00:00:26,663 --> 00:00:27,539
And remember,

17
00:00:27,539 --> 00:00:31,108
genuine employers do not ask for registration fees or

18
00:00:31,108 --> 00:00:32,994
security deposits for a job.

19
00:00:33,594 --> 00:00:34,368
And remember,

20
00:00:34,368 --> 00:00:36,275
if someone threatens you online,

21
00:00:36,275 --> 00:00:36,930
do not pay.

22
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:37,824
Save the chats,

23
00:00:37,824 --> 00:00:39,730
block the account and report it.

24
00:00:39,730 --> 00:00:40,981
It is not your fault.

25
00:00:41,581 --> 00:00:45,332
The National Cyber Crime Helpline number is 1930.

26
00:00:45,932 --> 00:00:50,677
You can also report cybercrime online at cybercrime.gov.in.

